//! Port of `src/font/glyf_rasterize_png_test.zig`.
//!
//! STATUS: ported
//!
//! Visual regression test for [`glyf_rasterize`](super::glyf_rasterize):
//! renders glyph protocol payloads into an atlas and compares it with the
//! reference PNG `src/font/testdata/glyf_rasterize.png` (generated by the
//! Zig/z2d implementation).
//!
//! Port note: the Zig test compares the PNG bytes and then the pixels
//! exactly. This port rasterizes with tiny-skia instead of z2d (see
//! `glyf_rasterize`), and uses a different PNG encoder, so it compares the
//! decoded pixels and tolerates small anti-aliasing differences (the same
//! tolerance the sprite face uses for the z2d goldens). On failure, the
//! generated PNG and a diff PNG are written to the system temp directory
//! (Zig: the working directory).

#![cfg(test)]

